      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you are monitoring him, the absolute emergency signs to never ignore are sudden severe headaches, weakness or numbness on one side of the body, slurred speech, or if he becomes confused or unresponsive again. Persistent dizziness, worsening severe headache, or vomiting should also prompt an immediate call to emergency services. If any of these definitive neurological symptoms appear, do not hesitate to seek urgent medical care.",
      "source": "target",
